3. TRAINING PIPELINE
────────────────────
  Step 1: Base model download via Ollama
          $ ollama pull llama3.1:8b

  Step 2: Dataset preparation
          Convert dataset.us.jsonl to chat-ml format:
            {"messages": [{"role":"system","content":"..."},
                          {"role":"user","content":"<input JSON>"},
                          {"role":"assistant","content":"<output JSON>"}]}

  Step 3: Fine-tune with LoRA (using axolotl, llama-factory, or unsloth)
          Config:
            base_model: meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct
            lora_r: 16
            lora_alpha: 32
            lora_target_modules: [q_proj, v_proj, k_proj, o_proj]
            epochs: 3
            learning_rate: 2e-4
            batch_size: 4
            gradient_accumulation_steps: 4
            warmup_ratio: 0.03
            max_seq_length: 4096

  Step 4: Merge adapter + quantize to GGUF Q4_K_M
          $ python llama.cpp/convert.py --outtype q4_k_m

  Step 5: Deploy via Ollama Modelfile
          FROM ./bbea-q4_k_m.gguf
          PARAMETER temperature 0.3
          PARAMETER top_p 0.9
          PARAMETER num_ctx 4096
          SYSTEM "<system prompt>"

  Step 6: Validate against hold-out set (10% of dataset.us.jsonl)
          Metrics: closure_status exact-match, conduct_score F1, JSON validity

